  "letter": {
    "premise": "To every soul who showed up, stayed up late, gave up comfortable choices, and poured themselves into something that had never been made before —",
    "point": "thank you."
  },
  "quote": {
    "text": "A hero is an ordinary individual who finds the strength to persevere and endure in spite of overwhelming obstacles.",
    "emphasis": "persevere and endure",
    "attribution": "Christopher Reeve"
  },
  "reflection": {
    "eyebrow": "What happened in 2026",
    "countLabel": "people, artists, collectives and organisations made ODDfest 2026. Together.",
    "body": "Creative Week ran June 8–14. Partner events across Helsinki brought in more than 1,000 people. ODDference filled two days with 25 speakers and more than 30 sessions. Then ODDfest took Friday and Saturday — more than 150 acts, from Vanha Ylioppilastalo to Tavastia.\n\nNone of it was ODD's alone. Ten curators built the programme. Artists brought their own work, their own crews and their own crowds. Volunteers kept things calm when they got chaotic, and they did get chaotic. Partners and foundations put in money, rooms and trust before anyone knew how it would turn out.\n\nThe theme was Bravery. Turned out it wasn't just a theme.",
    "closing": "Every one of them is named below. That's the point."
  },
  "photoBreak": {
    "image": "../../assets/oddfest-2026/valerie-june.jpg",
    "alt": "A singer playing acoustic guitar on a flower-decked stage at Vanha"
  },
